            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Historic Peace Accord Signed in Geneva"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                167,
                332,
                203
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "BY CATHERINE MOREAU"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                205,
                243,
                221
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "GENEVA — After seventeen grueling rounds of negotiation spanning more than three years, delegations from the three neighboring republics signed a comprehensive peace agreement at the Palais des Nations on Wednesday, formally concluding a border conflict that had displaced nearly two million civilians since 2019."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                225,
                332,
                387
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "DECADES OF CONFLICT END\nThe treaty, brokered by a coalition of neutral mediators from five nations, establishes a demilitarized zone spanning 40 kilometers along the contested highland frontier and creates an independent verification commission staffed by 600 international observers. Both armies must complete withdrawal within 90 days."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                392,
                334,
                571
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Under the accord's economic provisions, a \\$4.8 billion reconstruction fund will finance the rebuilding of eleven shattered townships, the clearance of an estimated 28,000 landmines, and the restoration of cross-border rail links severed since the conflict's first months."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                577,
                334,
                707
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Humanitarian agencies caution that the path to durable peace remains fragile. Analysts note that lasting stability will depend on accountability for wartime abuses and the meaningful reintegration of displaced communities into local political life."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                45,
                713,
                334,
                843
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Continued on Page A6"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                48,
                848,
                238,
                866
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "UNITED NATIONS — A coalition of 38 industrialized nations pledged $12 billion in dedicated adaptation funding for vulnerable island nations during the closing session of the General Assembly's climate plenary on Tuesday."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                352,
                168,
                643,
                285
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "FUNDING DEAL REACHED\nThe pledge, scaled up from an earlier $7 billion draft, will underwrite sea walls, freshwater reservoirs, and managed-relocation programs across the Pacific and Indian Ocean archipelagos most threatened by rising seas."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                352,
                288,
                642,
                420
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Delegates from the Alliance of Small Island States welcomed the commitment but stressed that the funding must arrive swiftly and without the bureaucratic delays that have hobbled previous climate pledges."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                352,
                425,
                643,
                541
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Diplomats Expand Cross-Border Rail Pact"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                354,
                554,
                640,
                590
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "BY LENA HOFFMANN"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                354,
                593,
                527,
                609
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "VIENNA — Transport ministers from nine Central European states ratified an expanded rail cooperation framework intended to cut freight transit times by 22 percent and harmonize signaling standards across national networks."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                352,
                612,
                642,
                726
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "CONNECTIVITY BOOST The agreement commits signatories to 7,400 kilometers of track modernization by 2031 and establishes a joint procurement authority for rolling stock, which planners estimate will save 1.3 billion euros in combined purchasing costs."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                352,
                731,
                643,
                863
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "governments announced expanded refugee resettlement quotas for the coming year, collectively offering 210,000 places, a 15 percent increase over 2024 figures."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                662,
                170,
                951,
                252
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "HUMANITARIAN LIFT The expansion follows mounting pressure from resettlement agencies facing funding shortfalls and a global displacement figure that has now exceeded 114 million people for the first time in recorded history."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                662,
                256,
                952,
                372
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Central Banks Coordinate Currency Swap Lines"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 2
            },
            "bbox": [
                663,
                385,
                951,
                437
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "BY PRIYA NAIR"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                663,
                441,
                794,
                457
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "BASEL — Central banks from twelve major economies renewed and expanded their bilateral currency swap arrangements at a quarterly meeting of the Bank for International Settlements, seeking to insulate emerging-market currencies from volatility."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                662,
                458,
                951,
                590
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "LIQUIDITY SAFEGUARD The renewed facilities total $950 billion in available liquidity and extend through December 2026, providing a backstop for trade financing and reserves management."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                662,
                595,
                952,
                695
            ]
        },
